      "writtenOn": "2020-12-18T17:27:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right. Aditionally, TCPMv2 calls pd_set_input_current_limit() in PE_SNK_Evaluate_Capability state (there is call to pd_process_source_cap()), so TCPMv2 behaviour is similar to TCPMv1.\n\nDo you think charge manager shouldn\u0027t call pd_set_new_power_request() when running TCPMv2 stack? First call (when TCPMv2 is in Evaluate_Capability) is unnecessary, because TCPMv2 is actually transitioning to choosen voltage. In second case (TCPMv2 in Transition_Sink), we transitioned to that voltage actually.\n\nOn the other side many boards calls pd_set_input_current_limit() in their PD policies.",
